1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:03,840
The transaction is not the crime the network is

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,140
Suspicious activity hides in the hops around a payment

3
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:09,050
not in the wire itself

4
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:12,320
Corridor Watch takes the network as the case

5
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:15,360
One synthetic case shows the path

6
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:19,160
A rule on one transaction flags the wrong object

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:23,390
Cross-border mule and layering rings are not a single wire

8
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:28,040
Funds can arrive rest for minutes and leave under another purpose

9
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:30,960
A threshold cannot see that shared device

10
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:34,950
The bank is left an alert and no memory of the network

11
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:39,720
This console is the middle bank bank_SG

12
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:45,800
Case CW-MID-02 is $9,050

13
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,900
Singapore to the Philippines

14
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,400
Risk 91

15
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,160
Mule pass-through

16
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:53,080
The queue marks it partial

17
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:56,300
The badge reads Partial network observed

18
00:00:56,490 --> 00:00:59,720
Visibility is coverage not guilt

19
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:08,050
18 minutes earlier CW-MID-01 brought $9,200 in from India

20
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:12,360
On shared device D-MID-MULE

21
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:15,000
The object under review is the corridor

22
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:18,990
Corridor Watch constructs that corridor before a model speaks

23
00:01:19,010 --> 00:01:21,880
Ingest never calls Gemini

24
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:26,560
A 12-step investigation directed a cyclic graph DAG

25
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:31,240
loads the payment both profiles risk features shared devices

26
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:36,360
and the neighborhood then drafts a deterministic verdict from the evidence pack

27
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:38,480
On this case the pill is high

28
00:01:38,910 --> 00:01:40,440
91

29
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:43,790
The stated next step is a human decision

30
00:01:43,790 --> 00:01:45,940
not an automatic clear

31
00:01:46,090 --> 00:01:50,490
Downstream of the Philippines hop the graph keeps an unknown boundary

32
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:52,860
It does not invent a bank

33
00:01:53,050 --> 00:01:55,070
Gemini does not see the raw ledger

34
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,600
It receives that evidence pack

35
00:01:57,750 --> 00:02:01,240
At the model boundary account identifiers are tokens

36
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,560
not customer names

37
00:02:03,690 --> 00:02:08,240
Forced Gemini explains only the pack why the case looks this way

38
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:12,360
what is still unknown and what a person should check next

39
00:02:12,490 --> 00:02:16,120
The recommendation is to pause for an FIU lead

40
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:19,640
The model cannot hold escalate or freeze

41
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:23,560
The verdict carries a provenance chip Gemini tools

42
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:27,720
pre-fetch grounded fallback or gate fail

43
00:02:27,830 --> 00:02:31,260
If the grounding gate rejects the report the chip reads

44
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:34,440
Gate fail and the deterministic verdict stands

45
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:36,750
Evidence chips cite the pack

46
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:39,400
A claim has to point at one of them

47
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:42,760
Consequential actions stay with the FIU lead

48
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:47,560
Hold payment escalate and freeze account are refused for an analyst

49
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,360
Here the lead records hold payment

50
00:02:50,490 --> 00:02:52,480
The rail moves to FIU lead

51
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:56,600
That is a human authorization in this console

52
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:58,750
It is not a core banking freeze

53
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:00,600
Gemini recommended

54
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:02,360
A person decided

55
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:06,180
A confirming decision writes crime pattern DNA

56
00:03:07,130 --> 00:03:11,400
This network strengthens the multi-hop layering fingerprint in the library

57
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:15,720
Confirmed investigations become reusable memory for the next case

58
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,400
not a one-off alert

59
00:03:17,510 --> 00:03:19,960
The next network can match that fingerprint

60
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,960
The library holds the pattern

61
00:03:22,070 --> 00:03:23,380
The single wire does not

62
00:03:23,510 --> 00:03:26,360
The transaction is not the crime

63
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,240
The network is

64
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:32,200
CorridorWatch turns investigations into institutional memory

